From 4e32d265181be33edb4d68210cdd4a6664f8f7f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds-bootstrap <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:21:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] battle_hp_bar: include the data header from beside the file

src/battle/battle_hp_bar.c:450 includes "battle/battle_hp_bar_data.h", but
that header lives in src/battle/, not include/, and the port harness's include
path (like every other game source's) has no src/ entry. The decomp's own
makefile adds -Isrc, which is why MWCC finds it. GCC reports the fatal error
"battle/battle_hp_bar_data.h: No such file or directory" and compiles no body.

Under SDK_PORT_3DS include "battle_hp_bar_data.h", which is found relative to
the including file in both builds; the #else keeps the original spelling.
This is the only game header a source reaches through a src/-relative path.

Identity: with -I build/upstream/src added (the decomp's makefile path, needed
for the original spelling to resolve at all), gcc-10 -E -P without
SDK_PORT_3DS is byte-identical: 471771 bytes both, the #else branch includes
the same file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/battle/battle_hp_bar.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/battle/battle_hp_bar.c b/src/battle/battle_hp_bar.c
index a9b5fbd..1fead12 100644
--- a/src/battle/battle_hp_bar.c
+++ b/src/battle/battle_hp_bar.c
@@ -447,7 +447,13 @@ static const ManagedSpriteTemplate sSpriteTemplate_HpBarSafariOrPark = {
     .vramTransfer = 0
 };
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// The data header sits next to this file; the port's include path does not
+// add src/ (the decomp's own makefile does).
+#include "battle_hp_bar_data.h"
+#else
 #include "battle/battle_hp_bar_data.h"
+#endif
 
 static void BattleHpBar_LoadBoxResources(SpriteSystem *spriteSystem, SpriteManager *spriteManager, NARC *narc, PaletteData *plttData, int barType) {
     const ManagedSpriteTemplate *pRes = BattleHpBar_Util_GetHpBoxSpriteTemplate(barType);
